          %h1#section_table_of_contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#for_2dimensional_surfaces"} For 2-dimensional surfaces
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#rational_cohomology"} Rational cohomology
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#braid_groups"} Braid groups
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesHeisenbergHomology"} Heisenberg homology
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#finiteindex_subgroups"} Finite-index Subgroups
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesForOrbifolds"} For orbifolds
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a (oriented)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong mapping class group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopy
            classes of (orientation preserving)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X
          %p
            Often this is considered specifically for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            with punctures in which case a central role is played by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dehn+twists"} Dehn twists
          %p
            The mapping class group is of importance in many areas of geometry including study of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teichm%C3%BCller+spaces"} Teichmüller spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of surfaces, of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+groups"} free groups
            and in geometric and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+group+theory"} combinatorial group theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Dehn"} Max Dehn
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jakob+Nielsen"} Jakob Nielsen
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Thurston"} William Thurston
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"} David Mumford
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(X)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            formed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-topological+infinity-groupoids"} Euclidean topological geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}_0(X) \hookrightarrow \mathbf{Aut}(X)
            be the inclusion of the connected component of the identity.
          %p Then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi MCG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{MCG}(X) \coloneqq \mathbf{Aut}(X)/\mathbf{Aut}_0(X)
          %p
            is the corresponding
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            onto itself, modulo
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotopy"} isotopy
          %p
            This is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Aut}(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MCG(X) = \pi_0(Diff(X))
                  \\,.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a manifold with boundary
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial X
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#for_2dimensional_surfaces For 2-dimensional surfaces
          %p
            The mapping class group for 2-dimensional manifolds controls the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+complex+curves"} moduli stack of complex curves
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dehn-Nielsen-Baer+theorem"} Dehn-Nielsen-Baer theorem
            identifies the extended mapping class group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo ±
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG^{\pm}
            (including orientation-reversing diffeos) of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genuse
            with the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/outer+automorphisms"} outer automorphisms
            of its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo ±
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Out
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MCG^\pm(\Sigma^2_g)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  Out\big(
                  \\pi_1(\Sigma^2_g)
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            of mapping class groups for 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            may also be encoded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorially
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ribbon+graphs"} ribbon graphs
          %p
            One of the classical results is that the (oriented) mapping class group of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2/\mathbb{Z}^2 \cong (S^1)^2
            is isomorphic to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+linear+group"} special linear group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SL%282%2CZ%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi SL
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(\mathbb{R}^n/\mathbb{Z}^n) \cong SL_n(\mathbb{Z})
          %p
            Certain generators called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dehn+twists"} Dehn twists
            may be visualized as cutting a torus along a circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a\} \times S^1
            (or
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \times \{b\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\pi
            and reattaching the two ends.
          %p
            Another example is a 2-disk with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            punctures. The group of diffeomorphisms (fixing the boundary pointwise) modulo isotopy is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_n
          %p
            The relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            is as follows:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientable
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} bare homotopy type
              of its diffeomorphism group is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Diff
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi O
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 3
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %mi MCG
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi SO
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 3
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %msub
                                  %mi ℤ
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi SO
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 3
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        \\Pi(Diff(S^2)) &amp; \simeq \Pi(O(3))
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \simeq MCG(S^2)\times \Pi(SO(3))
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \simeq \mathbb{Z}_2 \times \Pi(SO(3))
                        \\end{aligned}
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Diff
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %mi MCG
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %msub
                                  %mi GL
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo ×
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        \\Pi(Diff(S^1 \times S^1))
                        \&amp; \simeq
                        MCG(S^1 \times S^1)\times \Pi(S^1 \times S^1 )
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \simeq GL_2(\mathbb{Z}) \times B(\mathbb{Z} \times\mathbb{Z})
                        \\end{aligned}
              %li
                %p
                  in all other cases all higher
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                  vanish:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi MCG
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Pi(Diff(\Sigma)) \simeq MCG(\Sigma)
          %p
            The first statement is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Smale58"}> Smale 58
            ), see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+eversion"} sphere eversion
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#EarleEells67"} Earle-Eells 67
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gramain73"} Gramain 73
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher12"} Hatcher 12
            for review and see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "diffeomorphism+group#HomotopyTypeForSurfaces"} diffeomorphism group – For surfaces
            for more.
          %p
            On equivalently using homeomorphisms instead of diffeomorphisms:
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Boldsen09"} Boldsen 2009
          %h3#rational_cohomology Rational cohomology
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with rational coefficients of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of the stable mapping class group of 2-dimensional manifolds (hence essentially the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+complex+curves"} moduli stack of complex curves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mumford%27s+conjecture"} Mumford's conjecture
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MadsenWeiss02"} Madsen-Weiss 02
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #MCGOfClosedOrientedSurfaces.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The mapping class group of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^2 = \Sigma^2_1
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SL%282%2CZ%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi SL
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    MCG(T^2) \,\simeq\, Sp_2(\mathbb{Z}) \,\simeq\, SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
                    \\,,
            %p
              and generally the mapping class group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^2_g
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} = g \in \mathbb{N}
              sits in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi g
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1
                    \\to
                    I_g
                    \\longrightarrow
                    MCG(\Sigma^2_g)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Sp_{2g}(\mathbb{Z})
                    \\to 1
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_{2g}(\mathbb{Z}) \coloneqq Sp_{2g}(\mathbb{R}) \cap GL_{2g}(\mathbb{Z})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Torelli+group"} Torelli group
            %p
              Here the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(\Sigma^2_g)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ;
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi g
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_1(\Sigma^2_g;\mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}^g \times \mathbb{Z}^g
              of the surface is through the defining action of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sp
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_2(\mathbb{Z})
          (reviewed by
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Morita07"} Morita 2007 §6
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#FarbMargalit12"} Farb &amp; Margalit 2012 §6
          %p
          #MappingClassGroupsOfNPuncturedSpheres.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The mapping class groups of the
              = succeed "-" do
